## Phase 2: Security Headers Implementation

### Enable with Helmet

The secure app.js already includes helmet. Default configurations protect against:
- X-Frame-Options (Clickjacking)
- X-Content-Type-Options (MIME sniffing)
- Strict-Transport-Security (HTTPS enforcement)
- Content-Security-Policy (XSS prevention)

### Custom CSP Configuration

For your specific needs, modify CSP headers:

```javascript
app.use(helmet.contentSecurityPolicy({
  directives: {
    defaultSrc: ["'self'"],
    scriptSrc: ["'self'", "cdn.example.com"],
    styleSrc: ["'self'", "'unsafe-inline'"], // Avoid inline styles in production
    imgSrc: ["'self'", "data:", "https:"],
    fontSrc: ["'self'", "fonts.googleapis.com"],
    connectSrc: ["'self'", "api.example.com"],
    frameSrc: ["'none'"], // Prevent embedding in iframes
    mediaSrc: ["'self'"],
    objectSrc: ["'none'"],
    upgradeInsecureRequests: [],
  },
}));
```

