## Phase 3: Authentication Implementation

### 3.1 Token Generation

For production, use bcrypt for password hashing:

```bash
npm install bcryptjs
```

```javascript
const bcrypt = require('bcryptjs');

// When storing password
const hashedPassword = await bcrypt.hash(password, 10);

// When verifying password
const isValid = await bcrypt.compare(providedPassword, hashedPassword);
```

### 3.2 Token Strategy

Use JWT with the following claims:

```javascript
const token = jwt.sign(
  {
    id: user.id,
    username: user.username,
    role: user.role,
    iat: Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000),
  },
  process.env.ACCESS_TOKEN_SECRET,
  {
    expiresIn: '15m', // Short-lived access tokens
    algorithm: 'HS256',
  }
);
```

### 3.3 Implement Refresh Tokens

```javascript
app.post('/refresh', (req, res) => {
  const { refreshToken } = req.body;

  if (!refreshToken) {
    return res.status(401).json({ error: 'Refresh token required' });
  }

  try {
    const decoded = jwt.verify(refreshToken, process.env.REFRESH_TOKEN_SECRET);

    const newAccessToken = jwt.sign(
      { id: decoded.id, username: decoded.username, role: decoded.role },
      process.env.ACCESS_TOKEN_SECRET,
      { expiresIn: '15m' }
    );

    res.json({ accessToken: newAccessToken });
  } catch (error) {
    res.status(403).json({ error: 'Invalid refresh token' });
  }
});
```

