# Secrets Management: Best Practices & Implementation Guide

## Problem with Current Approach (.env.test)

```
❌ INSECURE:
- Secrets in version control
- Same credentials across environments
- No audit trail
- No automatic rotation
- Plain text storage
- Single point of failure
```

---

## SOLUTION ARCHITECTURE

### Production Environment (AWS)

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│         AWS Secrets Manager                          │
│  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────┐  │
│  │ Database Credentials                          │  │
│  │ - Encrypted at rest (KMS)                     │  │
│  │ - Rotated every 30 days                       │  │
│  │ - Access logged to CloudTrail                 │  │
│  └───────────────────────────────────────────────┘  │
│  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────┐  │
│  │ API Keys (Stripe, Anthropic, Logfire)        │  │
│  │ - Encrypted at rest                           │  │
│  │ - Version history available                   │  │
│  │ - Recovery windows configured                 │  │
│  └───────────────────────────────────────────────┘  │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
         ↓
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│              Lambda/EC2/ECS Container               │
│  - Assumes IAM role with Secrets Manager access   │
│  - Caches secrets in memory (not on disk)         │
│  - Rotates on Lambda initialization                │
│  - NO secrets in environment variables             │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

---

## Implementation: Secrets Manager Wrapper

```javascript
// lib/secrets-manager.js
const AWS = require('aws-sdk');

class SecretsManager {
  constructor(options = {}) {
    this.client = new AWS.SecretsManager({
      region: options.region || process.env.AWS_REGION
    });

    this.cache = new Map();
    this.cacheTTL = options.cacheTTL || 3600000; // 1 hour
    this.cacheTimestamps = new Map();
  }

  /**
   * Retrieve secret with caching
   */
  async getSecret(secretId) {
    // Check cache
    const cached = this.cache.get(secretId);
    const timestamp = this.cacheTimestamps.get(secretId);

    if (cached && timestamp && Date.now() - timestamp < this.cacheTTL) {
      console.log(`[CACHE HIT] ${secretId}`);
      return cached;
    }

    try {
      console.log(`[FETCHING] ${secretId} from Secrets Manager`);

      const data = await this.client
        .getSecretValue({ SecretId: secretId })
        .promise();

      let secretValue;

      if ('SecretString' in data) {
        secretValue = JSON.parse(data.SecretString);
      } else {
        secretValue = Buffer.from(data.SecretBinary, 'base64');
      }

      // Cache the secret
      this.cache.set(secretId, secretValue);
      this.cacheTimestamps.set(secretId, Date.now());

      return secretValue;

    } catch (error) {
      console.error(`Error retrieving secret ${secretId}:`, error);
      throw error;
    }
  }

  /**
   * Get all secrets for application
   */
  async loadAllSecrets(secretIds) {
    const secrets = {};

    for (const id of secretIds) {
      secrets[id] = await this.getSecret(id);
    }

    return secrets;
  }

  /**
   * Clear cache (for testing/refresh)
   */
  clearCache(secretId = null) {
    if (secretId) {
      this.cache.delete(secretId);
      this.cacheTimestamps.delete(secretId);
    } else {
      this.cache.clear();
      this.cacheTimestamps.clear();
    }
  }
}

module.exports = SecretsManager;
```

