SECURITY FINDINGS - OWASP TOP 10 ANALYSIS
===============================================================================

1. MISSING AUTHENTICATION & AUTHORIZATION (OWASP #1 - Broken Access Control)
   Severity: HIGH

   Issue: 
   - /users endpoint returns sensitive user data without any authentication
   - No authorization checks - any unauthenticated user can access all endpoints
   - No rate limiting to prevent abuse

   Risks:
   - Unauthorized access to user data (PII exposure)
   - Information disclosure vulnerability
   - API abuse/DoS potential

   Recommendation:
   Implement authentication middleware:

   BEFORE (Vulnerable):
   app.get('/users', (req, res) => {
     res.json([...]);
   });

   AFTER (Secure):
   const authenticateToken = (req, res, next) => {
     const authHeader = req.headers['authorization'];
     const token = authHeader && authHeader.split(' ')[1];

     if (!token) return res.sendStatus(401);

     jwt.verify(token, process.env.ACCESS_TOKEN_SECRET, (err, user) => {
       if (err) return res.sendStatus(403);
       req.user = user;
       next();
     });
   };

   app.get('/users', authenticateToken, (req, res) => {
     // Additional authorization check
     if (req.user.role !== 'admin') {
       return res.status(403).json({ error: 'Forbidden' });
     }
     res.json([...]);
   });

===============================================================================

2. MISSING INPUT VALIDATION (OWASP #3 - Injection)
   Severity: MEDIUM-HIGH

   Issue:
   - No input validation on query parameters or request body
   - Although current endpoints don't accept input, potential for expansion
   - Missing validation schemas

   Risks:
   - SQL injection (if database is added)
   - NoSQL injection
   - Command injection
   - Path traversal

   Recommendation:
   Implement input validation middleware:

   BEFORE (Vulnerable - if endpoints expand):
   app.get('/users/:id', (req, res) => {
     const userId = req.params.id;
     db.query('SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ' + userId); // SQL Injection!
   });

   AFTER (Secure):
   const { body, param, validationResult } = require('express-validator');

   app.get('/users/:id',
     param('id').isInt().toInt(),
     (req, res) => {
       const errors = validationResult(req);
       if (!errors.isEmpty()) {
         return res.status(400).json({ errors: errors.array() });
       }
       const userId = req.params.id; // Safe, already validated
       // Use prepared statements
       db.query('SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ?', [userId]);
     }
   );

===============================================================================

3. MISSING SECURITY HEADERS (OWASP #1, #2 - A01:2021)
   Severity: MEDIUM

   Issue:
   - No Content Security Policy (CSP)
   - No X-Frame-Options header (clickjacking protection)
   - No X-Content-Type-Options header (MIME sniffing prevention)
   - No Strict-Transport-Security (HSTS)
   - No X-XSS-Protection
   - CORS not configured (overly permissive by default)

   Risks:
   - Clickjacking attacks
   - MIME-type sniffing attacks
   - Cross-site scripting (XSS) vulnerabilities
   - Man-in-the-middle attacks

