================================================================================
10. NO HTTPS ENFORCEMENT
================================================================================

VULNERABILITY: HTTP requests allowed

ATTACK SCENARIO - Man in the Middle:
```
User's Browser -> HTTP -> Network -> Attacker -> HTTP -> App
           (unencrypted connection - easy to intercept!)

Attacker can:
- Read auth tokens
- Read user data
- Inject malicious content
- Modify responses
```

SECURE FIX:
```javascript
// 1. Enforce HTTPS in app
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  if (process.env.NODE_ENV === 'production') {
    if (req.header('x-forwarded-proto') !== 'https') {
      return res.redirect(`https://${req.header('host')}${req.url}`);
    }
  }
  next();
});

// 2. Add HSTS header
app.use(helmet.hsts({
  maxAge: 31536000, // 1 year
  includeSubDomains: true,
  preload: true
}));

// 3. Infrastructure level: Redirect HTTP to HTTPS
// In nginx/Apache/Load balancer
# nginx example:
server {
  listen 80;
  server_name example.com;
  return 301 https://$server_name$request_uri;
}
```

