### Option B: HashiCorp Vault (Recommended for Enterprise)

**Install:**
```bash
npm install axios
```

**Implementation:**
```javascript
const axios = require('axios');

class VaultClient {
  constructor(vaultAddr, vaultToken) {
    this.vaultAddr = vaultAddr || process.env.VAULT_ADDR;
    this.vaultToken = vaultToken || process.env.VAULT_TOKEN;

    if (!this.vaultAddr || !this.vaultToken) {
      throw new Error('VAULT_ADDR and VAULT_TOKEN required');
    }
  }

  async getSecret(path) {
    try {
      const response = await axios.get(
        `${this.vaultAddr}/v1/${path}`,
        {
          headers: {
            'X-Vault-Token': this.vaultToken,
          }
        }
      );
      return response.data.data.data;
    } catch (error) {
      console.error('Vault error:', error.message);
      process.exit(1);
    }
  }
}

// Usage
const vault = new VaultClient();
const secrets = await vault.getSecret('secret/data/app/prod');
const JWT_SECRET = secrets.JWT_SECRET;
```

**Vault Setup:**
```bash
# Write secret to Vault
vault kv put secret/app/prod \
  JWT_SECRET="your-secret-key" \
  DATABASE_URL="postgresql://..."

# Read it back
vault kv get secret/app/prod
```

**Benefits:**
- ✅ Dynamic secrets generation
- ✅ Secret versioning & history
- ✅ Encrypted storage
- ✅ Automatic revocation
- ✅ Multi-authentication methods
- ✅ Advanced audit logging

