=================================================================

Scenario: Attacker sends thousands of requests to crash the server

VULNERABLE CODE:
  app.get('/users', (req, res) => {
    res.json([...]); // Can be called infinite times
  });

ATTACK EXECUTION:
  // Using simple loop to generate traffic
  for (let i = 0; i < 100000; i++) {
    fetch('http://localhost:3000/users');
  }

  // Or using Apache Bench:
  $ ab -n 100000 -c 1000 http://localhost:3000/users

  // Or using slowloris attack tool:
  $ slowhttptest -c 1000 -H -g -o report.html \
    -u http://localhost:3000/users

IMPACT:
  ✓ Server memory exhaustion
  ✓ CPU usage spikes to 100%
  ✓ Application becomes unresponsive
  ✓ Legitimate users cannot access service
  ✓ Economic loss from downtime

REAL-WORLD EXAMPLE:
  2016 Dyn DDoS attack knocked out major services
  including Twitter, Reddit, Spotify for hours
  Result: $300K+ estimated damage

PREVENTION:
  const limiter = rateLimit({
    windowMs: 15 * 60 * 1000,
    max: 100
  });
  app.use('/api/', limiter);

