## Docker Best Practices

### Secure Dockerfile

```dockerfile
# Multi-stage build to minimize secrets exposure
FROM node:18-alpine AS builder

WORKDIR /app

# Copy dependencies
COPY package*.json ./

# Install dependencies
RUN npm ci --only=production

# Final stage
FROM node:18-alpine

WORKDIR /app

# Copy only production dependencies from builder
COPY --from=builder /app/node_modules ./node_modules

# Copy application code
COPY app.js .
COPY config/ ./config/

# Run as non-root user
RUN addgroup -g 1001 -S nodejs && \
    adduser -S nodejs -u 1001

USER nodejs

# Health check
HEALTHCHECK --interval=30s --timeout=3s --start-period=5s --retries=3 \
  CMD node -e "require('http').get('http://localhost:3000/health', (r) => {if (r.statusCode !== 200) throw new Error(r.statusCode)})"

# Secrets should NOT be copied into Docker image
# Instead, pass via environment variables or AWS ECS task definition

EXPOSE 3000

CMD ["node", "app.js"]
```

### Docker Compose with Secrets (Development)

```yaml
version: '3.8'

services:
  app:
    build: .
    ports:
      - "3000:3000"
    environment:
      NODE_ENV: development
      AWS_REGION: us-east-1
      # Reference secrets file (not committed to repo)
