# Security Best Practices Quick Reference

## 🚨 Top 10 Security Rules for This Application

### 1. NEVER Commit Secrets
```javascript
// ❌ WRONG - Don't do this
DATABASE_URL=postgres://admin:PASSWORD@db:5432/prod

// ✅ RIGHT - Use environment variables
const dbUrl = process.env.DATABASE_URL;
```

### 2. Always Authenticate Protected Endpoints
```javascript
// ❌ WRONG - No authentication
app.get('/users', (req, res) => { ... });

// ✅ RIGHT - Require valid JWT
app.get('/users', verifyToken, (req, res) => { ... });
```

### 3. Validate & Sanitize All Input
```javascript
// ❌ WRONG - Direct user input
const search = req.query.search;
users.filter(u => u.name.includes(search));

// ✅ RIGHT - Validate and sanitize
[query('search').trim().isLength({ max: 100 })]
// Then use validationResult to check
```

### 4. Use Strong Passwords & Hashing
```javascript
// ❌ WRONG - Storing plaintext password
user.password = req.body.password;

// ✅ RIGHT - Use bcrypt
const bcrypt = require('bcrypt');
const hash = await bcrypt.hash(password, 10);
user.password = hash;
```

### 5. Implement Rate Limiting
```javascript
// ❌ WRONG - No rate limiting
app.post('/login', (req, res) => { ... });

// ✅ RIGHT - Rate limit authentication
const authLimiter = rateLimit({ max: 5, windowMs: 15 * 60 * 1000 });
app.post('/login', authLimiter, (req, res) => { ... });
```

### 6. Set Security Headers
```javascript
// ❌ WRONG - No security headers
app.use(express.json());

// ✅ RIGHT - Add helmet middleware
const helmet = require('helmet');
app.use(helmet());
```

### 7. Use HTTPS in Production
```javascript
// ❌ WRONG - Allow HTTP
app.listen(3000);

// ✅ RIGHT - Enforce HTTPS
if (process.env.NODE_ENV === 'production') {
  app.use((req, res, next) => {
    if (req.header('x-forwarded-proto') !== 'https') {
      res.redirect(`https://${req.header('host')}${req.url}`);
    } else next();
  });
}
```

### 8. Handle Errors Securely
```javascript
// ❌ WRONG - Expose error details
app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
  res.json({ error: err.message, stack: err.stack });
});

// ✅ RIGHT - Generic errors in production
app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
  res.status(err.status || 500).json({
    error: process.env.NODE_ENV === 'development' 
      ? err.message 
      : 'Internal Server Error'
  });
});
```

### 9. Log Security Events (Without Secrets)
```javascript
// ❌ WRONG - Logging sensitive data
console.log('Login attempt:', req.body);

// ✅ RIGHT - Log only necessary info
console.log(JSON.stringify({
  event: 'LOGIN_ATTEMPT',
  userId: user.id,
  ip: req.ip,
  timestamp: new Date().toISOString()
}));
```

### 10. Implement Authorization Checks
```javascript
// ❌ WRONG - No authorization
app.get('/users/:id', verifyToken, (req, res) => {
  res.json(getUser(req.params.id));
});

// ✅ RIGHT - Verify user can access this data
app.get('/users/:id', verifyToken, (req, res) => {
  if (req.user.id !== parseInt(req.params.id)) {
    return res.status(403).json({ error: 'Forbidden' });
  }
  res.json(getUser(req.params.id));
});
```

